Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||06-20-2000||02:25 AM||||Ok i have an 87 4 cylinder that has been the target of most of my extra money for a couple years now (not without pleading with the wife) so i was wondering what everyone does with the old v6 that they swap for the 8, i would be interested in knowing how to get one, and how hard the conversion would be to do?<BR>Next i have seen air intakes for the fiero's on the roof kinda cool but who has one and i want to see some and find out where to get one.<P>If you can answer that would be great<P><BR>by the way "say yes if some youngin at the gas bar wants to check your oil" pop the hood and watch his face, heeheehee <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>sick humor, <BR>btw my plate tite fit I am 6'4"||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-20-2000||03:09 AM||||OK here is the scoop on the Indy scoops  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> IRM sells one for $200. The only other place I have seen them is from a place that calls them SD4 street scoops. Here is their link, I don't know what they charge.<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A>  <P>Finding a used one is going to be difficult since most people that have them want them.<BR>I also heard that FOCOA use to have some but I don't know if they still have them or not<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-20-2000||09:23 AM||||Don't bother asking Oreif if you can have his.  He's coming over to my house soon to install his on my hood/trunk, repaint the scoop, etc, etc.  I think this will be happening tomorrow.<P>Yawn!  What a dream I had! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||06-20-2000||12:06 PM||||For V6 conversion, think you can plan on changing ECM, mounts and fuel pump, and transaxle if yours is the original equipment 5-speed.  Sounds like a lot of work, and down time, especially if you haven't done it before.  There used to be a Scott Barrett (sp - ?) homepage that talked about his conversion to a V6.  Not a religious experience of course   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>If you want to do it, check Michigan Fiero Club want ads.  There was a guy who had a Fiero V6 & trans. for sale.  Auburn, IN area.    <P>         <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||4
